WEBVTT

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:13.660
It sure is cold, isn't it? Iceland.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.160
Got that right. But...

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:19.500
It's SO pretty!

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.910
Looking like it doesn't bother you...

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:26.870
You grew up in a snowy area,
didn't you, Ribbon?

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.200
I'm so friggin' cold...

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.250
Well, I have a secret weapon.

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:32.500
Secret weapon?

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.250
Yeah. This!

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:39.790
Iori gave them to me. Before we left.

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:41.950
Listen up, Idiot Ribbon.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:45.500
I don't make mistakes,
and I'm not letting this get to me.

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:46.870
Y-yeah...

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:53.000
Cold is a girl's greatest enemy.
Wear these and beat the cold!

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:57.370
That's just like Iori, isn't it?

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:58.700
Yup.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.910
So I have to do my best!

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:06.410
I mean, if we find the fourth one,
we'll have another iDOL, right?

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:12.120
Then, maybe we won't have to fight to see
who gets to be the pilots.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.160
That's been your thinking?

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:17.620
You're right. Let's do our best.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.000
Yeah!

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.160
It seems they're here.

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:28.330
Well, well. Thank you all.

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:30.580
My apologies for being late.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:35.830
I'm Hibiki Saku from Mondenkind EU.

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:40.620
I'm Joseph Shingetsu from
Mondenkind Japan. It's a pleasure.

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:42.120
The pleasure is mine.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:46.040
Welcome to the land of ice and fire!

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.870
I've heard the S.O.S.

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:53.830
Have you finally heard it?

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:09.790
In a cutesy way

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:13.330
Impure or pure, which character?

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:16.160
Maybe they're the same

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:18.700
The love beat is opened up full throttle

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:23.700
I've noticed, this is a special mission... I've got it

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:30.120
I'll show you for real, because I'll make it come true

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:34.000
In a world that's pierced through the skies

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:40.910
I felt a strange emotion, I liked you in an instant!

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:46.000
I'm sure I'll win with a smile

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:49.330
Sure enough a smile is the right way

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:54.910
I was small and crying but I'll rise to the challenge

00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:57.250
I wonder what this palpitation is

00:02:57.250 --> 00:03:00.540
I need a little medical attention

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:08.620
This feeling of slight fever
could be your fault, S.O.S!

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:21.500
Niflheim

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:25.750
Looks like nothing's out of the ordinary.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:27.080
Really?!

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:32.830
Okay, so I can play with Epi now?

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:33.790
Yes.

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:37.500
All right! Wait for me, Epi!

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:41.250
And?

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.500
What about MY results?

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:46.080
No major problems, but...

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:48.330
Your metabolism is on the downswing.

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:52.290
There's a possibility your body temperature
could suddenly plummet.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:54.540
I should administer a stimulant.

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:57.870
Is that so?

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:03.000
Well, we are Bastards, after all.

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:07.500
Which is why we need
as much data as we can get.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:10.500
To give birth to our perfect mischling.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:17.620
Incidentally, an iDOL
core lies dormant in Iceland.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:19.870
There's no mistake of that, yes?

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:22.080
We have no reason to doubt the intel.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:26.080
Our informant is desperate for my affection.

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:29.450
Well then, please prepare to deploy.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:41.580
Iceland is split along the Eurasian
and North American Plates.

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:45.200
Normally, it is frequented by earthquakes.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.790
But for some reason, these past 20 years,

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:50.540
the earthquakes that should've
been occurring, haven't.

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:56.290
We of Mondenkind EU have been
investigating with this fact firmly in mind.

00:04:56.540 --> 00:05:01.620
Our results: We have found gravitational
irregularities in the area around Grímsfjall.

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:03.910
You're saying that's because of a core?

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:09.950
We believe nothing else could be such that
it could disturb the plates' movements.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.830
It's been 20 years, you're sure of that?

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:19.200
Yes. Therefore, we believe this is the
fifth one: the last iDOL, Hiems.

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:25.200
The Tempestas incident
was seven years ago.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:28.290
If this has been going on for 20, then...

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:29.750
Oh!

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:32.700
That's right. Unfortunately.

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:39.200
Let's do our utmost to recover the Hiems
that rests just below the surface.

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:41.500
I'm counting on you, Miss Futami.

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:43.000
Sir!

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:50.040
All right, now begins our mission
to find and recover the Hiems!

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:53.660
Ami, you join the local staff
on their search party.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:57.370
All operators will provide backup
for the search team.

00:05:58.040 --> 00:05:59.330
Haruka and Makoto,

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:03.700
you stay on 24-hour standby on
the chance that you become needed.

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:05.290
"On the chance"?

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:10.750
I don't really want to consider it,
but if it's learned that the Hiems is here...

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:13.540
Turiavita is sure to make their move.

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:18.950
If they seize the core, the balance of power
between us and them will shift.

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:24.250
We MUST prevent that. Got it?

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:27.000
I await the opportunity.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:29.830
We'll strike without mercy...

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:31.330
This time.

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:35.700
Indeed.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:37.870
Do your best.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:48.000
We know what's inside the core. It's Hiems.

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:51.660
Huh. This one hasn't
shown up before, huh?

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:52.750
Correct.

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:57.250
The final core, that no human has
yet touched... We MUST acquire it.

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:02.540
Hmph! The truth is, you want to go
after the Imber, don't you?

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:06.370
You should just go! I'll go get Hiems.

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:09.250
Do you understand?
There can be no failure.

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:13.250
There's no need to worry! I mean...

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:16.410
Look who I've got with me.

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:20.200
All right. I leave the core to you.

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:22.330
I'll get...

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:25.950
Imber!

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.580
The hell is this?!

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:33.330
I told you to change this out with
a cold-weather buffering unit, didn't I?!

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:37.950
We're doin' what ya said.
Don't go gettin' all pissy about it.

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:42.750
I told you to do it BEFORE I sortie!
You're too slow!

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:45.330
Look, Makoto, winter settings
are gonna change

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:47.750
depending on the weather
and the temperature.

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:50.120
So, calibratin' for actual conditions
is the best way, right?

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:55.620
What's up with you? Normally,
you would've clicked to that right away.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:08:00.200
I just want things ready
and in optimal condition!

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:03.950
I need this TOOL to move when it counts!

00:08:07.870 --> 00:08:10.950
Recently, Makoto has been
nothing but angry, huh?

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:16.700
Yeah. But I think I understand
how she feels, sort of.

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:19.080
She might be scared.

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:20.750
Scared?

00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:23.290
Of the Nebula?

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:27.450
Of not belonging anywhere.

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:30.080
Yukiho?

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:39.200
Makoto.

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:43.200
What? I'm busy.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:44.750
I heard from Ami.

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:48.540
Your harmonizing levels are falling again.

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:52.540
What, that? There's been no change
to my overall motion capabilities.

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:57.160
I'd rather not be scolded over
the results of that hocus-pocus.

00:08:58.250 --> 00:09:00.950
I produce results. You have
no complaint with that, right?

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:01.500
That's-

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:02.290
Ma'am!
That's-

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:05.790
Please come. There's been word
from the search party.

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:08.250
They may have found the Hiems!

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:14.910
I think this may be it.

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:17.540
But it's quite deep.

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:23.200
Buried within a volcanic
magma deposit, eh?

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:25.330
That's rather tricky.

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:27.080
We'll force-activate the core.

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:31.700
If we awaken it, I think we can get
more precise confirmation. But...

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:33.950
You don't know what will happen?

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:35.290
Yes.

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:39.120
Why don't we just recover it?

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:44.160
Final authority lies with our director.
You're just the observer; please be quiet.

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:46.410
You're exactly right...

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:50.620
But the guys upstairs are clamoring
for this to get done.

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:55.370
Also, I get the feeling things will
get bad if we don't hurry.

00:09:56.250 --> 00:09:57.500
Picking up radar activity!

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:00.870
An object thought to be
an iDOL is approaching!

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:02.580
Well, well...

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:03.620
There are two!

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:04.750
TWO?!

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:05.830
Why are there two of them?

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:09.620
There's no time for questions.
We're ready to sortie, yes?

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:11.120
Of course.

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:15.500
Prometheus 1, Prometheus 2,
prepare to deploy.

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:16.540
Ma'am!

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:18.830
They're movin' out! No dilly dallyin'!

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:19.750
Ma'am!

00:10:20.410 --> 00:10:23.040
Ami, get as far away
from there as possible.

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:25.290
We don't want to give away our point.

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:26.200
Understood.

00:10:31.410 --> 00:10:34.250
Imber, Nebula, deploy!

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:37.620
The first unknown is approaching!

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:39.000
From 9 o'clock!

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:52.540
Nubilum!

00:10:56.870 --> 00:10:57.700
And the other?

00:10:58.040 --> 00:10:59.950
It's headed for Grímsfjall.

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:01.000
Grímsfjall?!

00:11:03.620 --> 00:11:05.700
Makoto! You head there.

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:09.000
No! I will defeat the Nubilum!

00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:13.580
This is an order. If you disobey,
I'll remove you from the Nebula.

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:17.750
I...

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:31.870
Move, you piece of junk!

00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:38.500
Say, Imber...

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:41.790
You don't like that memory, right?

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:45.250
We'll always be together.

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:47.040
Let's do it!

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:01.540
Go!

00:12:15.910 --> 00:12:18.250
Where? Where is it?

00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:41.250
What's this?!

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:48.290
Ta-daa!

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:54.620
This is my new friend.
It's Epimetheus 1, aka Epi!

00:12:58.120 --> 00:12:59.660
That's...!

00:12:59.910 --> 00:13:02.080
An iDOL?! No...

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:04.870
It can't be. This...

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:07.870
Terrible sound!

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:09.700
Well, it's about that time.

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:11.120
Let's go!

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:32.500
Makoto! What is it?

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:34.330
Receiving footage from the search vehicle.

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:38.750
What is it? What is that?!

00:13:39.450 --> 00:13:40.620
It can't be...

00:13:41.790 --> 00:13:43.290
The Epimetheus series.

00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:47.000
A project from more than 40 years ago.

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:52.120
Man tried to create an iDOL
by his own hands.

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:55.160
Prof. Cayenne's research?

00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:59.450
And the person at the center of Turiavita...

00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:01.160
Teru Lo-Wu.

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:07.750
I don't care. It's just a fake, right?

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:10.290
There's no way I can lose!

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:15.120
That's right. You gotta come on!

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:23.450
Whoops! You suck!

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:38.450
Direct hit! Accumulated damage
is reaching dangerous levels!

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:41.290
Haruka!

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:42.660
Are you all right?

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:45.620
Yeah! But...

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:02.540
So clumsy. I...

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:05.200
I should...!

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:13.830
Scary isn't it, Imber? I'm scared, too. But...

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:17.290
Everyone's rooting for us. So...

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:19.700
Let's do our best, Imber!

00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:24.370
Not a very good situation, is it?

00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:26.160
Oh, dear.

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:31.000
Such... incredible discordance!

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:35.160
The timbre that various iDOLs
and their Masters create is...

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:37.910
It's echoing throughout this surface!

00:15:45.830 --> 00:15:47.160
Don't tell me...

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:49.330
They're resonating!

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:53.000
Sir! Please stop the fighting!

00:15:53.790 --> 00:15:54.870
At this rate...!

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:03.000
What?!

00:16:05.120 --> 00:16:06.080
What is this?

00:16:12.080 --> 00:16:13.080
Nebula!

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:18.950
My head's gonna split open!

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:20.660
What's going on?

00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:50.160
What? What is this?

00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:53.250
Imber? Imber!

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:55.000
What's the matter?

00:17:13.580 --> 00:17:17.000
Ow... It seems to have died down, yes?

00:17:17.370 --> 00:17:19.330
Is everyone all right?

00:17:19.790 --> 00:17:21.750
Still, what WAS that?

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:25.700
That earthquake and eruption right now.

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:28.330
It may have awakened...

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:30.410
The Hiems.

00:17:30.790 --> 00:17:32.330
What was that?!

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:35.700
What about communications with
the iDOLs? Are they still down?

00:17:36.040 --> 00:17:40.580
Well... We've detected a massive
electromagnetic disturbance...

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:45.290
That was amazing.

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:52.000
Just now, it was like
a birthing cry, a scream.

00:17:58.200 --> 00:17:59.330
Piece of junk!

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:01.830
The Nebula is frozen.

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:05.500
It looks like that sound
knocked him unconscious.

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:09.000
It's all right. It's only temporary.

00:18:09.370 --> 00:18:12.370
I'm sure he'll wake up in a little while.

00:18:16.580 --> 00:18:17.660
Imber...

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:27.790
Are you okay?

00:18:30.370 --> 00:18:31.620
Supervisor?

00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:41.410
Imber...

00:18:44.500 --> 00:18:46.000
Ah! Hold on!

00:18:46.290 --> 00:18:47.830
Please hold on!

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:57.080
You're sure this is all right...

00:18:57.080 --> 00:18:58.450
Chihaya?

00:18:58.790 --> 00:19:01.250
Yes, Father.

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:10.080
If this will make me able to pilot
the Imber, I'm fine with it.

00:19:10.160 --> 00:19:12.160
The procedure is perfect.

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:17.410
When you awaken, you sisters
will have become closer to them...

00:19:18.620 --> 00:19:21.330
You are being reborn as a Mischling.

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:25.040
Imber...

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:35.120
Haruka... Amami?

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:43.450
Why?

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:47.580
I escaped from the Nubilum,
which had become inoperable,

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:50.830
and was exploring the valley
when suddenly my body...

00:19:51.450 --> 00:19:53.790
Your metabolism is on the downswing.

00:19:53.870 --> 00:19:57.500
There's a possibility your body temperature
could suddenly plummet.

00:19:58.500 --> 00:19:59.830
This girl...

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:08.750
It was just as he said. How wonderful.

00:20:21.370 --> 00:20:24.950
Huh? Before I knew it, I...

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:29.040
Ah, thank goodness.

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:34.830
You're awake, huh? I was so surprised
when you suddenly collapsed.

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:38.120
Your body was cold as ice, so I-

00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:43.790
I get it. But if you stay like that,
you'll catch a cold.

00:20:46.870 --> 00:20:48.950
Ah, I'm sorry!

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:51.330
Um, could you get me my clothes?

00:20:52.410 --> 00:20:55.910
It seems that you rescued me. I'm grateful.

00:20:56.410 --> 00:20:59.700
It was nothing. Um...

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:06.250
I'm from Mondenkind EU.

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:10.040
I'm Chihaya. Chihaya Kisaragi.

00:21:10.250 --> 00:21:13.120
Oh, so you work with Mr. Saku!

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:14.290
Yes.

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:18.450
What?

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:21.580
Um, would you mind turning
around for a bit?

00:21:24.410 --> 00:21:26.330
Well, I'm glad you're all right.

00:21:26.830 --> 00:21:29.330
Your body was SO cold.

00:21:29.870 --> 00:21:34.200
Oh, I'm Haruka Amami.
From Mondenkind Japan.

00:21:34.370 --> 00:21:37.950
I've heard. You're an Idolmaster, aren't you?

00:21:39.410 --> 00:21:40.580
For the Imber.

00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:42.910
Yes!

00:21:56.330 --> 00:22:05.250
Like a saint that crosses the ages

00:22:05.250 --> 00:22:14.250
In what kind of loneliness did you cry?

00:22:14.250 --> 00:22:23.120
Stretching out to a star so far away

00:22:23.120 --> 00:22:31.660
Say, I'll depict my feelings, look up at the sky

00:22:33.290 --> 00:22:43.080
Dear boy, if I always look for you in my heart

00:22:43.080 --> 00:22:52.080
Ah, I'll release a light so strong it will envelop you

00:22:52.080 --> 00:23:01.000
That sparkling trail will be the guide for us both

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:12.620
Now, no matter where we look, we feel the truth

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:29.250
Preview
Muspelheim

00:23:26.830 --> 00:23:28.950
They say it's called "hardfiskur".

00:23:28.950 --> 00:23:31.410
And this, apparently, is "blodmor".

00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:31.540
Note: Icelandic foods; dried fish and blood sausage,
respectively.
Preview
Muspelheim

00:23:31.410 --> 00:23:34.200
Look. They say this is "lifrarpylsa".

00:23:31.540 --> 00:23:41.040
Preview
Muspelheim

00:23:34.450 --> 00:23:38.830
Whoa. Were you really looking forward
to eating Icelandic cuisine?

00:23:38.830 --> 00:23:40.080
Yes.
